msgid "/etc/profile.d/dircolors.sh"
msgstr "/etc/profile.d/dircolors.sh"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:279
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This script uses the <filename>~/.dircolors</filename> and "
"<filename>/etc/dircolors</filename> files to control the colors of file "
"names in a directory listing. They control colorized output of things like "
"<command>ls --color</command>.  The explanation of how to initialize these "
"files is at the end of this section."
msgstr ""
"Este conjunto de comandos sequenciados usa os arquivos "
"<filename>~/.dircolors</filename> e <filename>/etc/dircolors</filename> para"
" controlar as cores dos nomes de arquivos em uma listagem de diretório. Eles"
" controlam a saída gerada colorida de coisas como <command>ls "
"--color</command>. A explicação do como inicializar esses arquivos está ao "
"final desta seção."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:286
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/dircolors.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Setup for /bin/ls and /bin/grep to support color, the alias is in /etc/bashrc.\n"
"if [ -f \"/etc/dircolors\" ] ; then\n"
"        eval $(dircolors -b /etc/dircolors)\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"if [ -f \"$HOME/.dircolors\" ] ; then\n"
"        eval $(dircolors -b $HOME/.dircolors)\n"
"fi</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/dircolors.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Setup for /bin/ls and /bin/grep to support color, the alias is in /etc/bashrc.\n"
"if [ -f \"/etc/dircolors\" ] ; then\n"
"        eval $(dircolors -b /etc/dircolors)\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"if [ -f \"$HOME/.dircolors\" ] ; then\n"
"        eval $(dircolors -b $HOME/.dircolors)\n"
"fi</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:300
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:303
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/profile.d/extrapaths.sh"
msgstr "/etc/profile.d/extrapaths.sh"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:307
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This script adds some useful paths to the <envar>PATH</envar> and can be "
"used to customize other PATH related environment variables (e.g. "
"LD_LIBRARY_PATH, etc) that may be needed for all users."
msgstr ""
"Este conjunto de comandos sequenciados adiciona alguns caminhos úteis à "
"<envar>PATH</envar> e pode ser usado para personalizar outras variáveis de "
"ambiente relacionadas a PATH (por exemplo, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, etc) que "
"possivelmente sejam necessárias para todos(as) os(as) usuários(as)."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:312
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/extrapaths.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>if [ -d /usr/local/lib/pkgconfig ] ; then\n"
"        pathappend /usr/local/lib/pkgconfig PKG_CONFIG_PATH\n"
"fi\n"
"if [ -d /usr/local/bin ]; then\n"
"        pathprepend /usr/local/bin\n"
"fi\n"
"if [ -d /usr/local/sbin -a $EUID -eq 0 ]; then\n"
"        pathprepend /usr/local/sbin\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"if [ -d /usr/local/share ]; then\n"
"        pathprepend /usr/local/share XDG_DATA_DIRS\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"# Set some defaults before other applications add to these paths.\n"
"pathappend /usr/share/info INFOPATH</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/extrapaths.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>if [ -d /usr/local/lib/pkgconfig ] ; then\n"
"        pathappend /usr/local/lib/pkgconfig PKG_CONFIG_PATH\n"
"fi\n"
"if [ -d /usr/local/bin ]; then\n"
"        pathprepend /usr/local/bin\n"
"fi\n"
"if [ -d /usr/local/sbin -a $EUID -eq 0 ]; then\n"
"        pathprepend /usr/local/sbin\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"if [ -d /usr/local/share ]; then\n"
"        pathprepend /usr/local/share XDG_DATA_DIRS\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"# Set some defaults before other applications add to these paths.\n"
"pathappend /usr/share/info INFOPATH</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:333
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The <command>man</command> program automatically deduces the search path for"
" man pages by examining the content of the <envar>PATH</envar> variable, see"
" <ulink role='man' url='&man;manpath.5'>manpath(5)</ulink> for details.  "
"Setting the <envar>MANPATH</envar> variable may override the automatic "
"deduction, so the BLFS editors do not recommend setting it.  If you must set"
" it for any reason, it's better to start its value with a colon "
"(<literal>:</literal>), for example "
"<command>MANPATH=:/opt/somepkg/share/man:/opt/otherpkg/share/man</command> "
"so the paths listed in the <envar>MANPATH</envar> variable will be appended "
"to the automatically deduced value instead of overriding it."
msgstr ""
"O programa <command>man</command> deduz automaticamente o caminho de "
"pesquisa para páginas de manual examinando o conteúdo da variável "
"<envar>PATH</envar>; veja-se <ulink role='man' "
"url='&man;manpath.5'>manpath(5)</ulink> para detalhes. Configurar a variável"
" <envar>MANPATH</envar> possivelmente substitua a dedução automática, de "
"forma que os(as) editores(as) do BLFS não recomendam configurá-la. Se você "
"precisar configurá-la por qualquer motivo, é melhor iniciar o valor dela com"
" dois pontos (<literal>:</literal>), por exemplo "
"<command>MANPATH=:/opt/somepkg/share/man:/opt/otherpkg/share/man</command>, "
"de forma que os caminhos listados na variável <envar>MANPATH</envar> sejam "
"pospostos ao valor deduzido automaticamente em vez de substituí-lo."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:351
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:354
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/profile.d/readline.sh"
msgstr "/etc/profile.d/readline.sh"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:358
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This script sets up the default <filename>inputrc</filename> configuration "
"file. If the user does not have individual settings, it uses the global "
"file."
msgstr ""
"Este conjunto de comandos sequenciados configura o arquivo padrão de "
"configuração <filename>inputrc</filename>. Se o(a) usuário(a) não tiver "
"configurações individuais, ele usará o arquivo global."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:363
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/readline.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Set up the INPUTRC environment variable.\n"
"if [ -z \"$INPUTRC\" -a ! -f \"$HOME/.inputrc\" ] ; then\n"
"        INPUTRC=/etc/inputrc\n"
"fi\n"
"export INPUTRC</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/readline.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Set up the INPUTRC environment variable.\n"
"if [ -z \"$INPUTRC\" -a ! -f \"$HOME/.inputrc\" ] ; then\n"
"        INPUTRC=/etc/inputrc\n"
"fi\n"
"export INPUTRC</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:374
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:377
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/profile.d/umask.sh"
msgstr "/etc/profile.d/umask.sh"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:381
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Setting the <command>umask</command> value is important for security.  Here "
"the default group write permissions are turned off for system users and when"
" the user name and group name are not the same."
msgstr ""
"Configurar-se o valor do <command>umask</command> é importante para a "
"segurança. Aqui as permissões padrão de escrita do grupo são desligadas para"
" os(as) usuários(as) de sistema e quando o nome do(a) usuário(a) e o nome do"
" grupo não forem os mesmos."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:386
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/umask.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># By default, the umask should be set.\n"
"if [ \"$(id -gn)\" = \"$(id -un)\" -a $EUID -gt 99 ] ; then\n"
"  umask 002\n"
"else\n"
"  umask 022\n"
"fi</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/umask.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># By default, the umask should be set.\n"
"if [ \"$(id -gn)\" = \"$(id -un)\" -a $EUID -gt 99 ] ; then\n"
"  umask 002\n"
"else\n"
"  umask 022\n"
"fi</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:425
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:428
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/profile.d/i18n.sh"
msgstr "/etc/profile.d/i18n.sh"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:432
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This script sets an environment variable necessary for native language "
"support. A full discussion on determining this variable can be found on the "
"<ulink url=\"&lfs-root;/chapter09/locale.html\">Configuring the System "
"Locale</ulink> page."
msgstr ""
"Este conjunto de comandos sequenciados configura uma variável de ambiente "
"necessária para o suporte ao idioma nativo. Uma discussão completa acerca de"
" se determinar esta variável pode ser encontrada na página <ulink "
"url=\"&lfs-root;/chapter09/locale.html\">Configurando a Localidade do "
"Sistema</ulink>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:439
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/i18n.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Set up i18n variables\n"
"for i in $(locale); do\n"
"  unset ${i%=*}\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"if [[ \"$TERM\" = linux ]]; then\n"
"  export LANG=C.UTF-8\n"
"else\n"
"  export LANG=<replaceable>&lt;ll&gt;</replaceable>_<replaceable>&lt;CC&gt;</replaceable>.<replaceable>&lt;charmap&gt;</replaceable><replaceable>&lt;@modifiers&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"fi</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/i18n.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Set up i18n variables\n"
"for i in $(locale); do\n"
"  unset ${i%=*}\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"if [[ \"$TERM\" = linux ]]; then\n"
"  export LANG=C.UTF-8\n"
"else\n"
"  export LANG=<replaceable>&lt;ll&gt;</replaceable>_<replaceable>&lt;CC&gt;</replaceable>.<replaceable>&lt;charmap&gt;</replaceable><replaceable>&lt;@modifiers&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"fi</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:452
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/i18n.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Set up i18n variables\n"
"for i in $(locale); do\n"
"  unset ${i%=*}\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"if [[ \"$TERM\" = linux ]]; then\n"
"  export LANG=C.UTF-8\n"
"else\n"
"  source /etc/locale.conf\n"
"\n"
"  for i in $(locale); do\n"
"    key=${i%=*}\n"
"    if [[ -v $key ]]; then\n"
"      export $key\n"
"    fi\n"
"  done\n"
"fi</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/i18n.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Set up i18n variables\n"
"for i in $(locale); do\n"
"  unset ${i%=*}\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"if [[ \"$TERM\" = linux ]]; then\n"
"  export LANG=C.UTF-8\n"
"else\n"
"  source /etc/locale.conf\n"
"\n"
"  for i in $(locale); do\n"
"    key=${i%=*}\n"
"    if [[ -v $key ]]; then\n"
"      export $key\n"
"    fi\n"
"  done\n"
"fi</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:475
#, xml-text
msgid "Other Initialization Values"
msgstr "Outros Valores da Inicialização"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:478
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Other initialization can easily be added to the <filename>profile</filename>"
" by adding additional scripts to the <filename "
"class='directory'>/etc/profile.d</filename> directory."
msgstr ""
"Outra inicialização pode facilmente ser adicionada ao "
"<filename>profile</filename> adicionando-se conjuntos adicionais de comandos"
" sequenciados ao diretório <filename "
"class='directory'>/etc/profile.d</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:488
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:491
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/bashrc"
msgstr "/etc/bashrc"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:495
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Here is a base <filename>/etc/bashrc</filename>.  Comments in the file "
"should explain everything you need."
msgstr ""
"Aqui está um <filename>/etc/bashrc</filename> de base. Os comentários no "
"arquivo deveriam explicar tudo o que você precisa."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:499
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/bashrc &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/bashrc\n"
"# Written for Beyond Linux From Scratch\n"
"# by James Robertson &lt;jameswrobertson@earthlink.net&gt;\n"
"# updated by Bruce Dubbs &lt;bdubbs@&lfs-domainname;&gt;\n"
"\n"
"# System wide aliases and functions.\n"
"\n"
"# System wide environment variables and startup programs should go into\n"
"# /etc/profile.  Personal environment variables and startup programs\n"
"# should go into ~/.bash_profile.  Personal aliases and functions should\n"
"# go into ~/.bashrc\n"
"\n"
"# Provides colored /bin/ls and /bin/grep commands.  Used in conjunction\n"
"# with code in /etc/profile.\n"
"\n"
"alias ls='ls --color=auto'\n"
"alias grep='grep --color=auto'\n"
"\n"
"# Provides prompt for interactive shells, specifically shells started\n"
"# in the X environment. [Review the LFS archive thread titled\n"
"# PS1 Environment Variable for a great case study behind this script\n"
"# addendum.]\n"
"\n"
"NORMAL=\"\\[\\e[0m\\]\"\n"
"RED=\"\\[\\e[1;31m\\]\"\n"
"GREEN=\"\\[\\e[1;32m\\]\"\n"
"if [[ $EUID == 0 ]] ; then\n"
"  PS1=\"$RED\\u [ $NORMAL\\w$RED ]# $NORMAL\"\n"
"else\n"
"  PS1=\"$GREEN\\u [ $NORMAL\\w$GREEN ]\\$ $NORMAL\"\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"unset RED GREEN NORMAL\n"
"\n"
"# GnuPG wants this or it'll fail with pinentry-curses under some\n"
"# circumstances (for example signing a Git commit)\n"
"# Note that tty -s will \"succeed\" in LFS chroot environment so we cannot\n"
"# use -s instead of redirecting to /dev/null.\n"
"$(tty &amp;>/dev/null) &amp;&amp; export GPG_TTY=$(tty)\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/bashrc</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/bashrc &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/bashrc\n"
"# Written for Beyond Linux From Scratch\n"
"# by James Robertson &lt;jameswrobertson@earthlink.net&gt;\n"
"# updated by Bruce Dubbs &lt;bdubbs@&lfs-domainname;&gt;\n"
"\n"
"# System wide aliases and functions.\n"
"\n"
"# System wide environment variables and startup programs should go into\n"
"# /etc/profile.  Personal environment variables and startup programs\n"
"# should go into ~/.bash_profile.  Personal aliases and functions should\n"
"# go into ~/.bashrc\n"
"\n"
"# Provides colored /bin/ls and /bin/grep commands.  Used in conjunction\n"
"# with code in /etc/profile.\n"
"\n"
"alias ls='ls --color=auto'\n"
"alias grep='grep --color=auto'\n"
"\n"
"# Provides prompt for interactive shells, specifically shells started\n"
"# in the X environment. [Review the LFS archive thread titled\n"
"# PS1 Environment Variable for a great case study behind this script\n"
"# addendum.]\n"
"\n"
"NORMAL=\"\\[\\e[0m\\]\"\n"
"RED=\"\\[\\e[1;31m\\]\"\n"
"GREEN=\"\\[\\e[1;32m\\]\"\n"
"if [[ $EUID == 0 ]] ; then\n"
"  PS1=\"$RED\\u [ $NORMAL\\w$RED ]# $NORMAL\"\n"
"else\n"
"  PS1=\"$GREEN\\u [ $NORMAL\\w$GREEN ]\\$ $NORMAL\"\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"unset RED GREEN NORMAL\n"
"\n"
"# GnuPG wants this or it'll fail with pinentry-curses under some\n"
"# circumstances (for example signing a Git commit)\n"
"# Note that tty -s will \"succeed\" in LFS chroot environment so we cannot\n"
"# use -s instead of redirecting to /dev/null.\n"
"$(tty &amp;>/dev/null) &amp;&amp; export GPG_TTY=$(tty)\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/bashrc</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:544
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For more information on the escape sequences you can use for your prompt "
"(i.e., the <envar>PS1</envar> environment variable) see <command>info "
"bash</command> -- <emphasis role=\"strong\">Node: Printing a "
"Prompt</emphasis>."
msgstr ""
"Para mais informação acerca das sequências de escape que você pode usar para"
" o teu prompt (isto é, a variável de ambiente <envar>PS1</envar>), veja-se "
"<command>info bash</command> -- <emphasis role=\"strong\">Nó: Imprimindo um "
"Prompt</emphasis>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:553
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:556
#, xml-text
msgid "~/.bash_profile"
msgstr "~/.bash_profile"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:560
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Here is a base <filename>~/.bash_profile</filename>.  If you want each new "
"user to have this file automatically, just change the output of the command "
"to <filename>/etc/skel/.bash_profile</filename> and check the permissions "
"after the command is run. You can then copy <filename> "
"/etc/skel/.bash_profile</filename> to the home directories of already "
"existing users, including <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>, "
"and set the owner and group appropriately."
msgstr ""
"Aqui está um <filename>~/.bash_profile</filename> de base. Se você quiser "
"que cada usuário(a) novo(a) tenha esse arquivo automaticamente, apenas mude "
"a saída gerada do comando para o "
"<filename>/etc/skel/.bash_profile</filename> e verifique as permissões "
"depois que o comando for executado. Você pode, então, copiar o "
"<filename>/etc/skel/.bash_profile</filename> para os diretórios home dos(as)"
" usuários(as) já existentes, incluindo o(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>, e configurar o(a) proprietário(a) e o "
"grupo apropriadamente."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:569
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; ~/.bash_profile &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin ~/.bash_profile\n"
"# Written for Beyond Linux From Scratch\n"
"# by James Robertson &lt;jameswrobertson@earthlink.net&gt;\n"
"# updated by Bruce Dubbs &lt;bdubbs@&lfs-domainname;&gt;\n"
"\n"
"# Personal environment variables and startup programs.\n"
"\n"
"# Personal aliases and functions should go in ~/.bashrc.  System wide\n"
"# environment variables and startup programs are in /etc/profile.\n"
"# System wide aliases and functions are in /etc/bashrc.\n"
"\n"
"if [ -f \"$HOME/.bashrc\" ] ; then\n"
"  source $HOME/.bashrc\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"if [ -d \"$HOME/bin\" ] ; then\n"
"  pathprepend $HOME/bin\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"# Having . in the PATH is dangerous\n"
"#if [ $EUID -gt 99 ]; then\n"
"#  pathappend .\n"
"#fi\n"
"\n"
"# End ~/.bash_profile</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; ~/.bash_profile &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin ~/.bash_profile\n"
"# Written for Beyond Linux From Scratch\n"
"# by James Robertson &lt;jameswrobertson@earthlink.net&gt;\n"
"# updated by Bruce Dubbs &lt;bdubbs@&lfs-domainname;&gt;\n"
"\n"
"# Personal environment variables and startup programs.\n"
"\n"
"# Personal aliases and functions should go in ~/.bashrc.  System wide\n"
"# environment variables and startup programs are in /etc/profile.\n"
"# System wide aliases and functions are in /etc/bashrc.\n"
"\n"
"if [ -f \"$HOME/.bashrc\" ] ; then\n"
"  source $HOME/.bashrc\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"if [ -d \"$HOME/bin\" ] ; then\n"
"  pathprepend $HOME/bin\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"# Having . in the PATH is dangerous\n"
"#if [ $EUID -gt 99 ]; then\n"
"#  pathappend .\n"
"#fi\n"
"\n"
"# End ~/.bash_profile</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:600
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:603
#, xml-text
msgid "~/.profile"
msgstr "~/.profile"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:607
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Here is a base <filename>~/.profile</filename>. The comments and "
"instructions for using <filename class=\"directory\">/etc/skel</filename> "
"for <filename>.bash_profile</filename> above also apply here. Only the "
"target file names are different."
msgstr ""
"Aqui está um <filename>~/.profile</filename> de base. Os comentários e as "
"instruções para se usar o <filename class=\"directory\">/etc/skel</filename>"
" para o <filename>.bash_profile</filename> acima também se aplicam aqui. "
"Somente os nomes dos arquivos alvo são diferentes."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:613
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; ~/.profile &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin ~/.profile\n"
"# Personal environment variables and startup programs.\n"
"\n"
"if [ -d \"$HOME/bin\" ] ; then\n"
"  pathprepend $HOME/bin\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"# Set up user specific i18n variables\n"
"#export LANG=<replaceable>&lt;ll&gt;</replaceable>_<replaceable>&lt;CC&gt;</replaceable>.<replaceable>&lt;charmap&gt;</replaceable><replaceable>&lt;@modifiers&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"\n"
"# End ~/.profile</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; ~/.profile &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin ~/.profile\n"
"# Personal environment variables and startup programs.\n"
"\n"
"if [ -d \"$HOME/bin\" ] ; then\n"
"  pathprepend $HOME/bin\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"# Set up user specific i18n variables\n"
"#export LANG=<replaceable>&lt;ll&gt;</replaceable>_<replaceable>&lt;CC&gt;</replaceable>.<replaceable>&lt;charmap&gt;</replaceable><replaceable>&lt;@modifiers&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"\n"
"# End ~/.profile</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:630
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:633
#, xml-text
msgid "~/.bashrc"
msgstr "~/.bashrc"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:637
#, xml-text
msgid "Here is a base <filename>~/.bashrc</filename>."
msgstr "Aqui está um <filename>~/.bashrc</filename> de base."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:640
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; ~/.bashrc &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin ~/.bashrc\n"
"# Written for Beyond Linux From Scratch\n"
"# by James Robertson &lt;jameswrobertson@earthlink.net&gt;\n"
"\n"
"# Personal aliases and functions.\n"
"\n"
"# Personal environment variables and startup programs should go in\n"
"# ~/.bash_profile.  System wide environment variables and startup\n"
"# programs are in /etc/profile.  System wide aliases and functions are\n"
"# in /etc/bashrc.\n"
"\n"
"if [ -f \"/etc/bashrc\" ] ; then\n"
"  source /etc/bashrc\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"# Set up user specific i18n variables\n"
"#export LANG=<replaceable>&lt;ll&gt;</replaceable>_<replaceable>&lt;CC&gt;</replaceable>.<replaceable>&lt;charmap&gt;</replaceable><replaceable>&lt;@modifiers&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"\n"
"# End ~/.bashrc</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; ~/.bashrc &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin ~/.bashrc\n"
"# Written for Beyond Linux From Scratch\n"
"# by James Robertson &lt;jameswrobertson@earthlink.net&gt;\n"
"\n"
"# Personal aliases and functions.\n"
"\n"
"# Personal environment variables and startup programs should go in\n"
"# ~/.bash_profile.  System wide environment variables and startup\n"
"# programs are in /etc/profile.  System wide aliases and functions are\n"
"# in /etc/bashrc.\n"
"\n"
"if [ -f \"/etc/bashrc\" ] ; then\n"
"  source /etc/bashrc\n"
"fi\n"
"\n"
"# Set up user specific i18n variables\n"
"#export LANG=<replaceable>&lt;ll&gt;</replaceable>_<replaceable>&lt;CC&gt;</replaceable>.<replaceable>&lt;charmap&gt;</replaceable><replaceable>&lt;@modifiers&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"\n"
"# End ~/.bashrc</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:666
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:669
#, xml-text
msgid "~/.bash_logout"
msgstr "~/.bash_logout"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:673
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"This is an empty <filename>~/.bash_logout</filename> that can be used as a "
"template.  You will notice that the base <filename>~/.bash_logout "
"</filename> does not include a <userinput>clear</userinput> command.  This "
"is because the clear is handled in the <filename>/etc/issue</filename> file."
msgstr ""
"Este é um <filename>~/.bash_logout</filename> vazio que pode ser usado como "
"um modelo. Você perceberá que o <filename>~/.bash_logout</filename> de base "
"não inclui um comando <userinput>clear</userinput>. Isso é porque o clear é "
"manuseado no arquivo <filename>/etc/issue</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/config/profile.xml:680
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; ~/.bash_logout &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin ~/.bash_logout\n"
"# Written for Beyond Linux From Scratch\n"
